PROJECT CONTEXT — KHYRAT LEGAL CONTENT ENGINE
Snapshot date: 2026-10-10
Repository: https://github.com/mr-romel/khyrat-legal-content-engine
Branch: main
Purpose: multi-workflow Egyptian legal-content generation, social publishing, Blogger SEO/search-demand articles, engagement automation, branded Reels with Telegram review, plus marketplace/opportunity tooling.

IMPORTANT RESPONSE/ENGINEERING RULES
- User expects direct execution in the repository, not just generic advice.
- Speak Egyptian Arabic when responding to the user.
- Be direct about failures; never call a run successful unless the external publishing outcome is verified.
- Never expose credentials. Never ask user to paste OAuth/token/storage-state secrets into chat.
- Do not delete code as “unused” without checking imports, workflow references, script entrypoints and tests.
- Separate confirmed evidence from hypotheses.
- A green workflow/job is not proof of public publication.
- Idempotency is required: retries must not create duplicates.

PUBLISHING SCHEDULE CONTRACT
- Exactly one slot every calendar day.
- Cairo timezone.
- Variable but deterministic daily time, 10:00–22:00 inclusive.
- No even/odd-day restriction.
- Do not introduce duplicate scheduling logic in runtime wrappers.
- Acceptance: every calendar date exactly once; times in allowed range; deterministic per date; variable across dates.

CURRENT P0 BLOCKER — BLOGGER
Evidence from 2026-10-10 demand run:
- Gemini API returned 429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED due to free-tier quota; reported retry delay approximately 13 hours at that time.
- Blogger REST API OAuth refresh returned invalid_grant: token expired/revoked.
- UI fallback filled and verified the article title; publish-confirmation dialog disappeared.
- Dashboard showed multiple “(Untitled)” drafts and repeated article rows.
- Exact title did not have a verifiable published permalink.
- Google public HTML/search fallback returned 429 rate-limit interstitial.
- Workflow exited with code 1. Keyword map persisted afterwards, but this is not publishing success.
Action:
1. Refresh/reconnect Blogger OAuth securely; update GitHub secret BLOGGER_OAUTH_JSON.
2. Verify BLOGGER_UI_STORAGE_STATE_B64 if UI fallback remains enabled.
3. Use Blogger REST API post ID/permalink or Blogger feed/authenticated dashboard for verification; don't rely on Google search HTML.
4. Verify editor body/title autosave, confirmation, published status and canonical permalink.
5. Safely inspect/clean existing Untitled drafts/duplicates only after verifying IDs and content.
6. Require a real public permalink before marking PUBLISHED.
