CURRENT P1 BLOCKER — PHARAONIC IMAGES
src/image_generator.py already explicitly bans pharaonic/ancient Egypt imagery and includes negative prompt terms for pyramids, sphinx, temples, hieroglyphs, pharaoh, papyrus and ruins unless topic is antiquities.
Therefore do not assume the prompt simply lacks a ban. Trace actual flow:
post → visual_description creation → selected provider/model → output/cache path/hash → image QA exact final file → uploaded asset.
Hypotheses to test: visual_description is generic/wrong, another image path/provider is used, cached asset bypasses QA, QA prompt/result fails to hard-block the motif, or the uploaded image is not the file inspected.
Add safe diagnostics (row ID, description, provider/model, image SHA-256, QA score/decision/reasons, final URL; no credentials). Hard-reject ancient-Egypt imagery in final QA except when topic explicitly concerns antiquities.
Relevant:
- src/image_generator.py
- src/image_qa.py
- src/free_media.py
- src/blogger_worker.py
- .github/workflows/publish-scheduled.yml

GEMINI QUOTA
The demand article worker has a legal-source-based fallback, but fallback generation does not fix Blogger OAuth or permalink verification. A model rename may not fix project-wide quota. Use billing/raised quota or a separately configured provider, and require verified legal sources.

